Here is the commit message:
fixing errors: * Not able to unmount filesystem * Wrongly set
 isMounted variable during shutdown

Here is the root cause:
The native call `NativeMethods.DokanMain(...)` blocks for the entire duration the filesystem is mounted and only returns when it is unmounted (or fails to mount). The original code called this method synchronously and then executed `isMounted.set(true)` immediately afterward, meaning `isMounted` was never set to `true` while the filesystem was actually mounted — it would only be set after `DokanMain` returned (i.e., after unmounting or failure). As a result, when `shutdown()` was invoked while the filesystem was still mounted, `isMounted.get()` incorrectly returned `false`, so the code skipped calling `DokanRemoveMountPoint()` entirely (logging "already unmounted"), making it impossible to unmount the filesystem. Additionally, in the shutdown logic, `isMounted` was directly overwritten with the return value of `DokanRemoveMountPoint()`, which could incorrectly flip the mounted state tracking regardless of actual success/failure semantics.

